description: How cake& Storybook and the npm package reach production after component work
globs:
  - "src/cakeand/components/**"
  - "src/cakeand/components/**/*.stories.tsx"
  - ".storybook/**"
alwaysApply: false
---

When editing cake& components or Storybook config — or when asked how to
publish cake&, ship a version, or update cake.lenovo.com/storybook — read and
follow
[.claude/skills/storybook-publish-pipeline/SKILL.md](../../.claude/skills/storybook-publish-pipeline/SKILL.md).

Pages (Storybook + site) deploy on every `main` merge. The npm package does
**not**: run **Publish design system package** by hand, dry-run first, never
reuse a tag, never hand-edit `starter/context/`.

If the designer install path changes, update Introduction, Getting Started,
the Resources Devkit card, and README **Use it** together — step-by-step,
layman's terms. Getting Started is top-level Storybook docs (not under
Cake& Maintenance). Consumer release links currently go to
https://github.com/cake-admin/cakev2/releases#release-v4.2.3
The published package ships `stories/` and `context/` via build-package.mjs.
